WEBVTT

00:14:28.677 --> 00:14:31.938
You look in their eyes, and there's
something very important missing.

00:14:31.962 --> 00:14:33.114
CA: Yes.

00:14:33.138 --> 00:14:34.718
EG: Fear is part of our makeup.

00:14:34.742 --> 00:14:37.708
It's something that's inherent in us.
It's a protective device.

00:14:37.732 --> 00:14:42.025
And my experience with fear
is to permit it to exist,

00:14:42.049 --> 00:14:45.097
and then to figure out
how to work with it.

00:14:45.121 --> 00:14:47.453
To me, working with fear
is what courage is.

00:14:47.477 --> 00:14:50.860
I've never started any project
that I wasn't afraid

00:14:50.884 --> 00:14:52.151
during the entire thing.

00:14:52.175 --> 00:14:54.934
And the conversation that I have with fear

00:14:54.958 --> 00:14:58.144
is not to say, "You are
the death of creativity,

00:14:58.168 --> 00:15:00.413
and I can't be creative
because you exist,"